SPI1's CON: a write replaces the register. Upstream merged each write into
the stored value, so a bit, once written 1, could never be cleared: after
any write with bit 13 (the transfer-done interrupt enable), every later
transfer raised interrupt 16, even after CON was written with bit 13 clear.
The JieLi SDK clears CON bits with ordinary writes, so on the chip CON reads
back as last written. Bit 14 (clear pending) is still a strobe, not stored.
Reported upstream by the owner (harness/upstream/fm1-emu-spi1-con.md).

--- a/crates/fm1-soc/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/fm1-soc/src/lib.rs
@@ -402,8 +402,9 @@
                 if value & 0x4000 != 0 {
                     self.periph.spi1_pending = false;
                 }
-                let stored = self.sfr_get(addr);
-                self.sfr_set(addr, (stored & !0x4000) | (value & !0x4000));
+                // a write replaces CON (bit 14 is a strobe, not stored): merging it into the
+                // stored value kept bit 13 set once any write had set it
+                self.sfr_set(addr, value & !0x4000);
             }
             0x11d04 => self.sfr_set(addr, value), // BAUD
             0x11d08 => {
